WEBVTT

1
00:00:26.083 --> 00:00:30.291


2
00:00:30.291 --> 00:00:31.416
<b>Here, </b>

3
00:00:31.416 --> 00:00:34.333
<b>Lord Krishna is shaking up Arjuna.</b>

4
00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:36.000
<b>He says,</b>

5
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.541
<b>"O Partha,</b>

6
00:00:37.541 --> 00:00:40.458
<b>do not act in such an unmanly manner.</b>

7
00:00:40.458 --> 00:00:43.083
<b>It does not befit you at all.</b>

8
00:00:43.083 --> 00:00:47.416
<b>Abandon this petty weakness and rise up."</b>

9
00:00:48.041 --> 00:00:52.291


10
00:00:52.291 --> 00:00:55.708
<b>From the use of such</b>
<b>disparaging words for Arjuna, </b>

11
00:00:55.708 --> 00:00:57.375
<b>do not think that</b>

12
00:00:57.375 --> 00:01:00.041


13
00:01:00.041 --> 00:01:02.916
<b>The Lord never loses composure.</b>

14
00:01:02.916 --> 00:01:09.583
<b>His effort is only to awaken the Kshatriya</b>
<b>within Arjuna by striking at his core.</b>

15
00:01:09.583 --> 00:01:16.541
<b>Rebuking a great warrior for</b>
<b>being unmanly questions his Kshatriya spirit.</b>

16
00:01:16.541 --> 00:01:23.375
<b>By simply calling Arjuna's compassion towards</b>
<b>the unrighteous a petty weakness,</b>

17
00:01:23.375 --> 00:01:28.583
<b>Lord Krishna makes it clear that Arjuna should</b>
<b>not remain under the false notion</b>

18
00:01:28.583 --> 00:01:32.000
<b>that showing mercy to sinners is a great deed.</b>

19
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:33.875
<b>At the same time,</b>

20
00:01:33.875 --> 00:01:37.708
<b>the Lord also addresses Arjuna as Partha,</b>

21
00:01:37.708 --> 00:01:38.375
<b>Pritha</b>

22
00:01:38.375 --> 00:01:41.166
<b>meaning the son of Kunti, Parth.</b>

23
00:01:41.166 --> 00:01:47.250
<b>By saying this, he reminds Arjuna of his</b>
<b>great lineage and his valor.</b>

24
00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:49.000
<b>Reproach on one hand,</b>

25
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:52.375
<b>and a mention of the valor of</b>
<b>his lineage on the other.</b>

26
00:01:52.375 --> 00:01:56.500
<b>The effort of both is to encourage Arjuna.</b>

27
00:01:57.125 --> 00:02:01.333


28
00:02:01.333 --> 00:02:03.541
<b>Arjuna believes that</b>

29
00:02:03.541 --> 00:02:09.583
<b>killing those standing on the enemy side is a sin</b>

30
00:02:09.583 --> 00:02:10.583
<b>because</b>

31
00:02:10.583 --> 00:02:13.000
<b>they are his own people. </b>

32
00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:23.208
<b>He argues that doing so will lead to the</b>
<b>destruction of the family and chaos.</b>

33
00:02:23.208 --> 00:02:26.875
<b>He is simply confused.</b>

34
00:02:26.875 --> 00:02:31.041
<b>At this moment, his mind is becoming weak,</b>

35
00:02:31.041 --> 00:02:32.291
<b>but he</b>

36
00:02:32.291 --> 00:02:35.166
<b>is unable to see it.</b>

37
00:02:35.166 --> 00:02:37.958
<b>Not being able to recognize one's weaknesses  </b>

38
00:02:37.958 --> 00:02:44.208
<b>is one of the greatest</b>
<b>shortcomings of human beings.</b>

39
00:02:44.208 --> 00:02:45.375
<b>Just as</b>

40
00:02:45.375 --> 00:02:53.416
<b>many people consider their lack of restraint</b>
<b>not as a weakness but as a strength,</b>

41
00:02:53.416 --> 00:02:54.791
<b>they say that </b>

42
00:02:54.791 --> 00:02:58.875
<b>restraint is a symbol of slow pace.</b>

43
00:02:58.875 --> 00:02:59.708
<b>On the other hand,</b>

44
00:02:59.708 --> 00:03:01.750
<b>some people who quickly lose their temper</b>

45
00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:10.708
<b>and say anything to anyone believe</b>
<b>that this is a symbol of fearlessness.</b>

46
00:03:10.708 --> 00:03:13.250
<b>That they are outspoken</b>

47
00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:14.083
<b>because</b>

48
00:03:14.083 --> 00:03:18.541
<b>they are not afraid of anyone.</b>

49
00:03:18.541 --> 00:03:22.583
<b>This is a great irony of human nature.</b>

50
00:03:22.583 --> 00:03:25.458
<b>If one does not know their weaknesses, </b>

51
00:03:25.458 --> 00:03:29.791
<b>how can they correct them?</b>

52
00:03:29.791 --> 00:03:31.250
<b>So how</b>

53
00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:34.750
<b>can one know their flaws  </b>

54
00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:37.958
<b> and weaknesses?</b>

55
00:03:37.958 --> 00:03:39.291
<b>There</b>

56
00:03:39.291 --> 00:03:42.083
<b>are two ways:</b>

57
00:03:42.083 --> 00:03:44.500
<b>Difficult challenges.</b>

58
00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:51.208
<b>Just as a movie can be watched repeatedly,</b>

59
00:03:51.208 --> 00:03:59.833
<b>consider how you reacted to</b>
<b>a past difficult challenge. </b>

60
00:03:59.833 --> 00:04:02.875
<b>Think on it.</b>

61
00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:04.041
<b>Were you</b>

62
00:04:04.041 --> 00:04:06.833
<b> disturbed?</b>

63
00:04:06.833 --> 00:04:10.500
<b>What kind of thoughts</b>
<b>were coming to your mind? </b>

64
00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:16.541
<b>By reviewing all this during a peaceful time,</b>
<b>you will be able to know</b>

65
00:04:16.541 --> 00:04:18.375
<b>what deficiency</b>

66
00:04:18.375 --> 00:04:22.041
<b>needs to be worked on.</b>

67
00:04:22.041 --> 00:04:23.791
<b>The second way is</b>

68
00:04:23.791 --> 00:04:30.125
<b>to seek advice from someone</b>
<b>who is your well-wisher </b>

69
00:04:30.125 --> 00:04:34.083
<b>and who knows you closely.</b>

70
00:04:34.083 --> 00:04:35.291
<b>A guru</b>

71
00:04:35.291 --> 00:04:36.708
<b>or teacher,</b>

72
00:04:36.708 --> 00:04:38.000
<b>a friend,</b>

73
00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:39.333
<b>parents,</b>

74
00:04:39.333 --> 00:04:41.083
<b>siblings.</b>

75
00:04:41.083 --> 00:04:47.875
<b>They will tell you the truth</b>
<b>without any vested interest.</b>

76
00:04:47.875 --> 00:04:55.416
<b>By thus knowing your weaknesses,</b>
<b>strive to remove them.</b>

77
00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:00.291


78
00:05:00.291 --> 00:05:05.375
<b>I'm criticizing Arjun here,</b>

79
00:05:05.375 --> 00:05:06.791
<b>but</b>

80
00:05:06.791 --> 00:05:11.541
<b>he won't take offense.</b>

81
00:05:11.541 --> 00:05:16.125
<b>Our bond is unique</b>

82
00:05:16.125 --> 00:05:19.083
<b>built on affection</b>

83
00:05:19.083 --> 00:05:21.125
<b>and trust.</b>

84
00:05:21.125 --> 00:05:24.666
<b>No matter how heated our debates</b>

85
00:05:24.666 --> 00:05:28.541
<b>or how harsh my words may seem,</b>

86
00:05:28.541 --> 00:05:37.458
<b>he knows my intentions are pure.</b>

87
00:05:37.458 --> 00:05:39.458
<b>Some people's</b>

88
00:05:39.458 --> 00:05:45.416
<b>words, though sharp, don't sting us at all.</b>

89
00:05:45.416 --> 00:05:55.916
<b>While others speak sweet as honey,</b>
<b>yet we sense hidden barbs or motives. </b>

90
00:05:55.916 --> 00:05:57.375
<b>So what </b>

91
00:05:57.375 --> 00:06:00.791
<b>should we focus on?</b>

92
00:06:00.791 --> 00:06:02.708
<b>The words spoken</b>

93
00:06:02.708 --> 00:06:09.000
<b>or the intent behind them?</b>

94
00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:11.250
<b>Truth be told,</b>

95
00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:15.125
<b>more important than both</b>

96
00:06:15.125 --> 00:06:20.708
<b>is your relationship with the person.</b>

97
00:06:20.708 --> 00:06:22.750
<b>When conversing,</b>

98
00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:26.833
<b>we rarely dissect every word</b>

99
00:06:26.833 --> 00:06:36.791
<b>or have time to unravel hidden meanings.</b>

100
00:06:36.791 --> 00:06:39.833
<b>We trust certain individuals,</b>

101
00:06:39.833 --> 00:06:44.000
<b>so their words never taste bitter.</b>

102
00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:45.041
<b>And</b>

103
00:06:45.041 --> 00:06:52.875
<b> trust isn't built on words or weighing intentions. </b>

104
00:06:52.875 --> 00:07:00.375
<b>It's forged over time, hand in hand with honesty.</b>

105
00:07:00.375 --> 00:07:04.125
<b>Be genuine in your conduct, </b>

106
00:07:04.125 --> 00:07:08.416
<b>invest time in relationships,</b>

107
00:07:08.416 --> 00:07:12.166
<b>and they'll naturally grow strong.</b>

108
00:07:12.708 --> 00:07:16.791


109
00:07:16.791 --> 00:07:21.208
<b>Life will present moments</b>

110
00:07:21.208 --> 00:07:25.833
<b>when you'll feel like Arjun.</b>

111
00:07:25.833 --> 00:07:30.041
<b>Times when everything seems pointless.</b>

112
00:07:30.041 --> 00:07:35.250
<b>You'll want to drop it all and run. </b>

113
00:07:35.250 --> 00:07:40.125
<b>When it feels like you're losing to yourself.</b>

114
00:07:40.125 --> 00:07:47.500
<b>This is part and parcel of the</b>
<b>human experience, my friend.</b>

115
00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:52.583
<b>Arjun desperately needs me now.</b>

116
00:07:52.583 --> 00:07:57.708
<b>And with me by his side, he won't lose.</b>

117
00:07:57.708 --> 00:07:59.625
<b>He'll rise,</b>

118
00:07:59.625 --> 00:08:02.458
<b> and I'll be there to lift him up</b>

119
00:08:02.458 --> 00:08:08.583
<b>even if it means being tough on him.</b>

120
00:08:08.583 --> 00:08:11.833
<b>I'll guide you too,</b>

121
00:08:11.833 --> 00:08:14.708
<b>through this Gita.</b>

122
00:08:14.708 --> 00:08:17.375
<b>But</b>

123
00:08:17.375 --> 00:08:26.125
<b>in person, who is that individual</b>
<b>whom you consider your guru in life? </b>

124
00:08:26.125 --> 00:08:29.458
<b>Whom do you regard as your guide?</b>

125
00:08:29.458 --> 00:08:35.541
<b>Whose bitter advice is also for your benefit?</b>

126
00:08:35.541 --> 00:08:39.291
<b>Recognize the value of these guides.</b>

127
00:08:39.291 --> 00:08:43.875
<b>If no name springs to mind, </b>

128
00:08:43.875 --> 00:08:45.583
<b>then rethink,</b>

129
00:08:45.583 --> 00:08:52.125
<b>seek out those with experience, who know you, </b>

130
00:08:52.125 --> 00:08:54.625
<b>who have your best interests at heart.</b>

131
00:08:54.625 --> 00:08:58.166
<b>Keep these people close.</b>

132
00:08:58.166 --> 00:09:00.125
<b>When doubt creeps in</b>

133
00:09:00.125 --> 00:09:03.750
<b>or you lose faith in yourself,</b>

134
00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:08.958
<b>these mentors will surely come to your aid.</b>

